cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "validation-gate: a gate that refuses the shortcuts behind irreproducible claims"
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, in a due-diligence report, or in any
  published or client-facing analysis, please cite it and credit the author.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Corrêa Bezerra"
    given-names: "Cleiton Augusto"
    email: augusto.cleiton@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/cleitonaugusto/validation-gate"
url: "https://cleitonaugusto.github.io/validation/"
abstract: >-
  A validation gate for machine learning in science. It enforces hash-sealed
  pre-registration, a mandatory trivial baseline that must be beaten in the
  declared direction, a blind holdout counted in a ledger so a second run is
  refused, and paired bootstrap confidence intervals on the gain over the
  baseline. It reports four verdicts rather than two: a holdout under 30 points
  returns INCONCLUSIVE instead of being called a pass. Built by auditing the
  author's own computational-chemistry research, where it passed zero of five
  benchmarks.
keywords:
  - validation
  - reproducibility
  - pre-registration
  - baseline comparison
  - blind holdout
  - machine learning for science
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
